==============================================================================
O25 — compression curve  (exact psi, truncated explicit formula, no fitting)
==============================================================================
  psi(x)   = SUM_{p^k <= x} log p                       EXACT, from a sieve
  psi_K(x) = x - log(2pi) - (1/2)log(1 - x^-2)
             - 2 sqrt(x) SUM_{k<=K} [(1/2)cos(gL) + g sin(gL)]/(1/4 + g^2)
  L = log x, g = gamma_k, zeros paired as rho, conj(rho), rho = 1/2 + i gamma

  EVALUATED OFF THE DISCONTINUITIES: x_eval = x_int + 0.5, so no evaluation
  point is an integer and therefore none is a prime power, where psi jumps by
  log(p) and the explicit formula converges to the MIDPOINT of the jump.

  K_first(x, target) = the SMALLEST swept K with the error <= the target.
  K_stay (x, target) = the SMALLEST swept K such that EVERY swept K' >= K also
                       meets the target; null if the largest swept K fails.
  K_stay is the PRIMARY statistic: bands, crossover and the figure all use it.
  COMPRESSIVE at x : K_stay is not null AND K_stay <= pi(x).
  EXPANSIVE   at x : K_stay is null OR K_stay > pi(x).

  O10 is a DELIBERATE GAP in this series and is not filled here.

